t","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Resolved upstream before this change was pushed. Commit f2e4247a1 (\"tests: align hierarchy schema fixture with review phase\") applied the identical fix — adding review_phase to the old_shape fixture — and origin/main HEAD 7cec0f64c is now green (test_plan_review_hierarchy_incomplete.py: 12 passed). No separate change needed; closing as resolved-elsewhere/duplicate. Root-cause note retained here: the red landed via the Rebase-If-Necessary hazard (change 889 earned Verified+1 on a pre-test base, then merged server-side without re-running CI against the conflicting old_shape fixture).","timestamp":1784753050918270001},{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"FORCE_CLOSE: close gate(s) bypassed by user approval — no completion/signature attestation was signed. Reason: \"Fixed upstream by commit f2e4247a1 before this change was pushed; identical one-line fixture fix. origin/main HEAD green (12 passed). No commit references this ticket because the fix landed under another; closing as duplicate/resolved-elsewhere.\". Session: d96ad199-666f-460a-8d48-9e7792e1af7e.","timestamp":1784753193563949001}],"created_at":1784752607706434001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Problem\n\n`main` (origin/main HEAD 94e605a29) is red: `tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_hierarchy_incomplete.py::test_precheck_output_schema_accepts_old_and_new_shapes` fails deterministically with `agent output failed schema 'plan_review_precheck_output': 'review_phase' is a required property`.\n\n## Root cause\n\nChange 889 (\"Add phased plan-review attestations\") made `review_phase` a **required** property of `plan_review_precheck_output.schema.json` — correctly, since the precheck now always emits it (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py:561,690,720`). The test's `old_shape` fixture, which predates that change and omits `review_phase`, was never updated. Change 889 earned `Verified +1` on a patch set based on a pre-test base; Rebase-If-Necessary merged it at submit without re-running CI, so the semantically-broken combination landed green (ADR 0047 hazard).\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd `\"review_phase\": \"planning\"` to the `old_shape` dict in `test_precheck_output_schema_accepts_old_and_new_shapes`. The field is now always emitted, so the fixture was simply stale; `new_shape` (built via `**old_shape`) inherits it. No production code changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `old_shape` in `test_precheck_output_schema_accepts_old_and_new_shapes` includes `\"review_phase\": \"planning\"`, matching the now-required schema property.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_hierarchy_incomplete.py` passes against origin/main src (all 12 tests green).\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass.\n- [ ] No production/schema files are changed — the fix is test-only (the schema requirement is intentional).\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Change lands through Gerrit with `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_hierarchy_incomplete.py","reason":"add review_phase to old_shape fixture to match now-required schema property"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a1771f16-4106-4b1c-a351-9c636028e469","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ec20-c34a-b8ad-4d58","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Fix red main: stale old_shape fixture omits now-required review_phase","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["cbedf599-a7e4-4030-8af1-444f939d7f42","d8aba483-8c3b-40c4-9a61-8a61d15b2423","2a0a190b-ab2b-428d-84f9-0e550cb63a2d","fae22a59-5626-4402-a7eb-1d05d72